# Rank 1658 / CVE-2025-55182: the Flight reply deserializer resolved a
# client-supplied "$id:seg:seg" outline reference by walking the
# deserialized objects one segment at a time with a plain subscript,
# so a reference such as $3:constructor:constructor reached through
# the prototype chain to the Function constructor, and a crafted
# Promise-like .then resolves via the chunk wake path --
# unauthenticated remote code execution on any Server Function
# endpoint (CVSS 10.0; the React blog post and Dynatrace's analysis
# name the missing attribute check). The walk in getOutlinedModel
# (packages/react-server/src/ReactFlightReplyServer.js) ran
# `value = value[path[i]]` with no own-property check, where path is
# reference.split(':') and reference is a slice of the reply model
# string; loadServerReference then handed metaData.id to
# resolveServerReference/requireModule with no typeof check. Pool
# The fixing commit 7dc903cd29 ("Patch FlightReplyServer with
# fixes from ReactFlightClient (#35277)", 822 lines in this file):
# both walk sites now read
# `if (typeof value === 'object' && hasOwnProperty.call(value, name))`,
# loadServerReference rejects a non-string id, getChunk and
# resolveStream take only string FormData entries, and the wake loops
# invoke only typeof-function listeners. Remediation verified present
# at the fixed revision.
#
# ATTENTION, two stacked gaps.
#
# 1. Engine, frontend: a function whose signature carries Flow-only
# type syntax extracts nothing at all. The plain JavaScript grammar
# errors on the generic parameter (getOutlinedModel<T>) and on union
# parameter types (reference: void | string), and the whole function
# -- calls, subscripts, its analysis.function.context -- drops from
# the graph. Measured on the real file: 30 top-level functions yield
# 14 contexts (one named, thirteen empty lambdas); getOutlinedModel,
# parseModelString, reviveModel and loadServerReference yield zero
# nodes (`vyql query -call` reports 0 for each), so `vyql match` on
# the file reports no source, no sink and no control. Minimal pair:
# `function walk<T>(ref: string): T` gives zero contexts where
# `function walk(ref: string)` gives one with the split and the
# subscript walk visible; a sibling function is unaffected, so the
# loss is per function, not file-wide. The .ts route through the same
# shared walker extracts the generic signature with the walk tokens
# present, which is the shape of the change (route Flow-annotated .js
# through the TypeScript grammar). ENGINE-GAPS.md entry reported.
#
# 2. Vocabulary, provenance: even with extraction, the segments come
# from reference.split(':') where reference is a slice of the reply
# model string -- the untrusted-property-name family of ranks 1518,
# 1584 and 1613. Nothing labels the delimiter-separated names of a
# wire format as untrusted, and the control half exists:
# own_property_key_guard=true fires on the patched walk (verified
# against the frontend on the fixed file's shape), so only the
# positive half is missing. A guard-free presence binding over
# split+subscript walks is unshippable: the reachable set is 15 of
# 168 split-carrying files on next.js, 38 of 266 on lime-survey and
# 35 of 181 on microweber, and the hits are vendored browser
# libraries (ace editor workers, jquery.sparkline, highcharts) whose
# walks read trusted config paths. No definition change shipped.
#
# Measured on the real code: zero findings at both revisions (the
# whole-tree scan reports 2060 findings, none in this file).
# Spec cve_rank1658 records the unguarded walk and the
# own-property-guarded form, both asserting reject VYQL-INJ-013:
# when Flow signatures extract and untrusted-name provenance lands,
# the unguarded form must flip to expect.

test "rank1658: the outline walk follows the prototype chain"
  lang javascript
  file packages/react-server/src/ReactFlightReplyServer.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  function getOutlinedModel<T>(
    response: Response,
    reference: string,
    parentObject: Object,
    key: string,
    map: (response: Response, model: any) => T,
  ): T {
    const path = reference.split(':');
    const id = parseInt(path[0], 16);
    const chunk = getChunk(response, id);
    switch (chunk.status) {
      case INITIALIZED:
        let value = chunk.value;
        for (let i = 1; i < path.length; i++) {
          value = value[path[i]];
        }
        return map(response, value);
      default:
        throw chunk.reason;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1658: the fixed revision reads only own properties on the walk"
  lang javascript
  file packages/react-server/src/ReactFlightReplyServer.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  function getOutlinedModel<T>(
    response: Response,
    reference: string,
    parentObject: Object,
    key: string,
    map: (
      response: Response,
      model: any,
      parentObject: Object,
      key: string,
    ) => T,
  ): T {
    const path = reference.split(':');
    const id = parseInt(path[0], 16);
    const chunk = getChunk(response, id);
    switch (chunk.status) {
      case INITIALIZED:
        let value = chunk.value;
        for (let i = 1; i < path.length; i++) {
          const name = path[i];
          if (
            typeof value === 'object' &&
            hasOwnProperty.call(value, name)
          ) {
            value = value[name];
          }
        }
        return map(response, value, parentObject, key);
      default:
        throw chunk.reason;
    }
  }
  ```
